[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493960 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6da77181-6032-5e5c-929d-4a017fc0454f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493553}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6da77181-6032-5e5c-929d-4a017fc0454f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493553} :answer-field/id #uuid "5932016c-ec0a-5d79-9f39-b11ee0e695a8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493826}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d4dc1b86-0478-57c7-a48b-3ee42621256c" :question/math-academy-id "q-175957" :question/problem "Expressed as an integer, $(-4)÷\\left(\\frac{2}{5}\\right)\\times 6=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nWe multiply and divide, from left to right:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-4)÷\\frac{2}{5}\\times 6 &= ((-4)÷\\frac{2}{5})\\times 6 \\\\ &= (\\frac{-4}{1}\\times \\frac{5}{2})\\times 6 \\\\ &= \\left(\\frac{(-4)\\times 5}{1\\times 2}\\right)\\times 6 \\\\ &= \\left(-\\frac{20}{2}\\right)\\times 6 \\\\ &= (-10)\\times 6 \\\\ &= -60\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493961 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d681392-0578-56c7-9fe2-42e3d7339e02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493615}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d681392-0578-56c7-9fe2-42e3d7339e02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493615} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2d075a9-50ba-561b-90ab-b8b2901e72d8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493872}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d59d88c8-9c62-51d9-bd12-48f5c362cc67" :question/math-academy-id "q-352652" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x+1}{{sec}^{3}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.$ Substituting this into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x+1}{{sec}^{3}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{3}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493962 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "264f5867-7c47-5f07-9b9c-b3815c6cd840" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "53.10\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493452} {:answer/id #uuid "73143a86-4466-59b0-9d13-697c03f90f7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40.50\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493562} {:answer/id #uuid "975eb98b-4ab0-5014-8bea-9fcf9cfaaba5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50.50\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493630} {:answer/id #uuid "ec6926a3-0298-524c-9ffa-d17531745d04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52.15\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493768} {:answer/id #uuid "ff5d72e2-1423-5d98-a00f-6cea45e898da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48.05\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493801}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "975eb98b-4ab0-5014-8bea-9fcf9cfaaba5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50.50\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493630} :answer-field/id #uuid "7782954d-0945-5a09-a4ad-d4eaf2acb6cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493839}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d916a01a-c116-520b-be92-bf93eddd6997" :question/math-academy-id "q-95126" :question/problem "The lengths of babies at birth in a given population are normally distributed with a mean of $\\mu \\,\\text{cm}$ and a standard deviation of $6\\,\\text{cm}.$ Additionally, the length of $60%$ of the newborns falls between $0.9\\mu \\,\\text{cm}$ and $1.1\\mu \\,\\text{cm}.$ Find the mean $\\mu $ rounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p$ is given below, where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.75\\,$ | $\\,0.80\\,$ | $\\,0.85\\,$ | $\\,0.90\\,$ | $\\,0.95\\,$ | $\\,0.97\\,$ | $\\,0.99\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,0.6745\\,$ | $\\,0.8416\\,$ | $\\,1.0364\\,$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ | $\\,1.8808\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the length of a randomly selected newborn. Then we have $X∼N(\\mu ,{6}^{2}),$ and we want to find the mean $\\mu .$ \n\nWe know that $P(0.9\\mu <X<1.1\\mu )=0.6.$ First, we convert this to a cumulative probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0.9\\mu <X<1.1\\mu ) & =0.6 \\\\ 2P(\\mu <X<1.1\\mu ) & =0.6 \\\\ P(\\mu <X<1.1\\mu ) & =0.3 \\\\ P(X<\\mu )+P(\\mu <X<1.1\\mu ) & =0.5+0.3 \\\\ P(X<1.1\\mu ) & =0.8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we convert $X$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<1.1\\mu ) & =0.8 \\\\ P(Z<\\frac{0.1\\mu }{6}) & =0.8 \\\\ Φ\\left(\\frac{0.1\\mu }{6}\\right) & =0.8 \\\\ \\frac{0.1\\mu }{6} & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, \n\n$$\n{Φ}^{-1}(0.8)≈0.8416.\n$$\n\nFinally then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{0.1\\mu }{6} & =0.8416 \\\\ 0.1\\mu  & =5.0496 \\\\ \\mu  & =\\frac{5.0496}{0.1} \\\\  & ≈50.50\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493970 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63e7cc4a-4887-5d31-b8e4-aff9bc110c7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493542}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63e7cc4a-4887-5d31-b8e4-aff9bc110c7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493542} :answer-field/id #uuid "97f65a01-cb5a-533f-b4b2-586e85f00033" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493850}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e22ccace-d75b-5bc7-acc2-7090937bcda1" :question/math-academy-id "q-324457" :question/problem "In a distribution center, the average weight of shipped packages is $2.5$ kilograms. However, $20%$ of packages weigh no more than $2.3$ kilograms. Assuming that package weights are normally distributed, find the standard deviation, $\\sigma ,$ of the package weights, **rounded to two decimal places.**\n\n*Hint: A table of values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p$ is given below, where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.10\\,$ | $\\,0.15\\,$ | $\\,0.20\\,$ | $\\,0.25\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,-2.3263\\,$ | $\\,-1.8808\\,$ | $\\,-1.6449\\,$ | $\\,-1.2816\\,$ | $\\,-1.0364\\,$ | $\\,-0.8416\\,$ | $\\,-0.6745\\,$ |\n\n$\\sigma ≈$\n{{field-1}}\n$kg$" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the package weight (in kilograms). Then we have $X∼N(2.5,{\\sigma }^{2}),$ and we want to find the standard deviation $\\sigma .$ \n\nWe know that $P(X\\le 2.3)=0.20.$ Converting $X$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2.3) & =0.20 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{2.3-2.5}{\\sigma }) & =0.20 \\\\ Φ\\left(-\\frac{0.2}{\\sigma }\\right) & =0.20 \\\\ -\\frac{0.2}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.20).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, \n\n$$\n{Φ}^{-1}(0.20)=-0.8416.\n$$\n\nFinally then, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{0.2}{\\sigma } & =-0.8416 \\\\ \\frac{0.2}{\\sigma } & =0.8416 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{0.2}{0.8416} \\\\  & ≈0.24\\,\\text{kg}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493973 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "143bd49e-b2ca-5b56-9eca-6d7751d7c1e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493428} {:answer/id #uuid "37392f66-38d1-5cf1-a83a-b61ffbecdc24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493480} {:answer/id #uuid "3b9d745e-3b7a-5566-acd4-df51a55a0434" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493492} {:answer/id #uuid "757701d0-e96c-58b7-9b6d-52ab1067ccc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493565} {:answer/id #uuid "f8b8b11d-0fcd-5a7a-8d95-67c9db317553" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "143bd49e-b2ca-5b56-9eca-6d7751d7c1e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493428} :answer-field/id #uuid "b260735c-8ce2-5820-82bd-e9db5e7533a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493865}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e9c37ee3-304c-5283-97a5-75391f3d1e94" :question/math-academy-id "q-82985" :question/problem "Using the change of variables $u=x+3y$ and $v=x+2y,$ evaluate the double integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\frac{x+3y}{x+2y}\\,dx\\,dy,\n$$\n\nwhere $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x+3y\\le 2,\\,2\\le x+2y\\le 4\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v),y(u,v))|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|du\\,dv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x+3y,\\,v=x+2y\n$$\n\n \n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uv$-plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,2\\le v\\le 4\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & \\text{ }\\text{ }2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={\\left(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)}\\right)}^{-1}=-1.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{x+3y}{x+2y}\\,dx\\,dy & ={∬}_{Δ}\\frac{u}{v}\\cdot |\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}\\frac{u}{v}\\cdot |-1|\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{u}{v}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}u[{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{v}\\,dv]du \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}u[\\operatorname{ln}⁡v]_{2}^{4}\\,du \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}u(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)\\,du \\\\  & =(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2){\\int }_{0}^{2}u\\,du \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2[\\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot (2-0) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493975 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4f2613b-7acb-5604-981e-e17f2565df89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4f2613b-7acb-5604-981e-e17f2565df89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493785} :answer-field/id #uuid "bee0cd22-295e-5274-8db9-3430efc1f645" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493870}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fe644563-13d6-5255-adb7-59462252c8b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-325123" :question/problem "The average amount of coffee dispensed into medium cups is $10$ ounces. Additionally, in $15%$ of cups, the coffee amount is less than $9.1$ ounces. Assuming the amount dispensed is normally distributed, find the percentage of cups containing less than $8.5$ ounces of coffee. **Round your answer to two decimal places.**\n\n*Hint: A table of values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p$ is given below, where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution.*\n\n| $\\,p\\,$ | $0.01$ | $0.03$ | $0.05$ | $0.10$ | $0.15$ | $0.20$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,-2.3263\\,$ | $\\,-1.8808\\,$ | $\\,-1.6449\\,$ | $\\,-1.2816\\,$ | $\\,-1.0364\\,$ | $\\,-0.8416\\,$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n*In addition, you're given the following table of values for $p=Φ(z).$*\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-1.8\\,$ | $\\,0.0344\\,$ | $\\,0.0336\\,$ | $\\,0.0329\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.7\\,$ | $\\,0.0427\\,$ | $\\,0.0418\\,$ | $\\,0.0409\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.6\\,$ | $\\,0.0526\\,$ | $\\,0.0516\\,$ | $\\,0.0505\\,$ |\n\nApprximately\n{{field-1}}$%$ of cups contain less than $8.5$ ounces of coffee." :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the amount of coffee in a randomly selected cup. Then we have $X∼N(10,{\\sigma }^{2}),$ and we want to find $P(X<8.5).$ But first, we need to find the standard deviation $\\sigma .$\n\nWe know that $P(X<9.1)=0.15.$ First, we convert $X$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<9.1) & =0.15 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{9.1-10}{\\sigma }) & =0.15 \\\\ Φ\\left(\\frac{-0.9}{\\sigma }\\right) & =0.15 \\\\ \\frac{-0.9}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.15).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, \n\n$$\n{Φ}^{-1}(0.15)=-1.0364.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-0.9}{\\sigma } & =-1.0364 \\\\ \\frac{0.9}{\\sigma } & =1.0364 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{0.9}{1.0364} \\\\ \\sigma  & ≈0.8684.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve for $P(X<8.5)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<8.5) & =P(X\\le 8.5) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le \\frac{8.5-10}{0.8684}) \\\\  & ≈P(Z\\le -1.73) \\\\  & =Φ(-1.73) \\\\  & =0.0418 \\\\  & ≈4.18%.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, approximately $4.18%$ of coffee cups contain less than $8.5$ ounces of coffee."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495050 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f14cc015-61de-559e-9d6e-4f7e934ed9c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln(2x)+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f14cc015-61de-559e-9d6e-4f7e934ed9c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln(2x)+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494890} :answer-field/id #uuid "a47a029c-812d-5ac8-b753-06da557530dc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494995}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "02602311-35ef-53b7-9d8d-d64db15f3075" :question/math-academy-id "q-341724" :question/problem "Given that $y={\\left(\\frac{1}{2x}\\right)}^{x}$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-{(2x)}^{-x}\\cdot ($\n{{field-1}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "We have the function \n\n$$\ny={\\left(\\frac{1}{2x}\\right)}^{x}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we take the natural logarithm of both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({\\left(\\frac{1}{2x}\\right)}^{x}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{1}{2x}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{1}{2x}\\right)) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot {y}^{′} & =(x)^{′}\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{1}{2x}\\right))+(x)\\cdot {(\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{1}{2x}\\right))}^{′} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot {y}^{′} & =1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{1}{2x}\\right)+x\\cdot ((2x)\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{2}{(2x)^{2}}\\right)) \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{1}{2x}\\right)-1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for ${y}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =-y(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y={\\left(\\frac{1}{2x}\\right)}^{x}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =-{\\left(\\frac{1}{2x}\\right)}^{x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1) \\\\  & =-{(2x)}^{-x}\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495056 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03fe396d-fe54-5331-9b0d-89cca76e8a83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494325} {:answer/id #uuid "28e4f656-f65d-5411-8d23-3582c6860ee1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494395} {:answer/id #uuid "7e76872b-704c-5f0c-a9ff-08c0e8fdc198" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494593} {:answer/id #uuid "93ee67a5-c7ed-59bc-a55b-a2b9816ca144" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{17}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494657} {:answer/id #uuid "a652b819-cc60-593b-be0f-164896bc2a59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494698}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93ee67a5-c7ed-59bc-a55b-a2b9816ca144" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{17}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494657} :answer-field/id #uuid "df747204-bd95-5057-9f83-9ee058a01322" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495026}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0f15a926-c445-59e0-9b0e-24fb3d26db90" :question/math-academy-id "q-99830" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\frac{8}{x}+\\frac{2}{4x}$ for $x=-5.$" :question/worked-solution "We replace $x$ with $-5$ in the expression and simplify as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{x}+\\frac{2}{4x} &= \\frac{8}{(-5)}+\\frac{2}{4\\cdot (-5)} \\\\ &= -\\frac{8}{5}+\\left(-\\frac{2}{20}\\right) \\\\ &= -\\frac{8}{5}-\\frac{1}{10} \\\\ &= -\\frac{16}{10}-\\frac{1}{10} \\\\ &= \\frac{-16-1}{10} \\\\ &= -\\frac{17}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495059 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76a2fca9-a004-56dc-bcb9-7a9d56bf96b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494570} {:answer/id #uuid "807c89b0-1baf-5d8a-afd4-cecf678b8f6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494600} {:answer/id #uuid "83e55904-4dad-5f50-9ed8-a699c5c350a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494608} {:answer/id #uuid "b4dca2c1-f3a5-573b-82d7-9841c885f465" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494739} {:answer/id #uuid "ebf26341-3745-5f43-a14c-cda67d69e390" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494880}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83e55904-4dad-5f50-9ed8-a699c5c350a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494608} :answer-field/id #uuid "91b5b4ea-2fbf-58c6-b385-fcfece3b9311" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494987}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "11be1c1c-7eab-52eb-aab8-c16c55806ef6" :question/math-academy-id "q-160917" :question/problem "Use a change of variables to evaluate the double integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\frac{y-2x}{y+2x}\\,dxdy,\n$$\n\nwhere $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y-2x\\le 2,\\,2\\le y+2x\\le 6\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dxdy={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v),y(u,v))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: Find a suitable change of variables.\n\nThe inequalities that define the region $D,$\n\n$$\n0\\le y-2x\\le 2,\\,2\\le y+2x\\le 6,\n$$\n\nsuggest that we use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=y-2x\\,\\text{and}\\,v=y+2x.\n$$\n\nThis change of variables gives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uv$-plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,2\\le v\\le 6\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ \\text{ }\\text{ }\\text{ }2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={\\left(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)}\\right)}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 5**: Perform the change of variables, and evaluate the integral:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{y-2x}{y+2x}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{Δ}\\frac{u}{v}\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}\\frac{u}{v}|-\\frac{1}{4}|\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}u[{\\int }_{2}^{6}\\frac{1}{v}\\,dv]du \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}u[\\operatorname{ln}⁡|v|]_{2}^{6}\\,du \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}u(\\operatorname{ln}⁡6-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)\\,du \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}u\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,du \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{4}{[\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495100 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36ad6cac-d25a-50df-a71c-ff5530463782" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494431} {:answer/id #uuid "377131c4-9276-5492-90f4-5fe9f9ea094b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494433} {:answer/id #uuid "389c158d-eca4-5138-ade2-702a2174ac43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(2\\pi -1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494436} {:answer/id #uuid "76f8296f-42f1-5d17-a5c6-7274b014898c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{12}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494571} {:answer/id #uuid "adfbcfe0-1ed2-552d-9eab-c92cbe93246a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{6\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76f8296f-42f1-5d17-a5c6-7274b014898c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{12}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494571} :answer-field/id #uuid "caaee621-928c-5865-8689-d0a675bcc7ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495012}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "75903bf3-d1b7-5813-a3cf-49663583fcbd" :question/math-academy-id "q-160915" :question/problem "Use a change of variables to evaluate the double integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi xy)\\,dxdy,\n$$\n\nwhere $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le xy\\le 4,\\,1\\le \\frac{y}{x}\\le 5\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dxdy={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v),y(u,v))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: Find a suitable change of variables.\n\nThe inequalities that define the region $D,$\n\n$$\n1\\le xy\\le 4,\\,1\\le \\frac{y}{x}\\le 5,\n$$\n\nsuggest that we use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=xy\\,\\text{and}\\,v=\\frac{y}{x}.\n$$\n\nThis change of variables gives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uv$-plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 4,\\,1\\le v\\le 5\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\text{ }\\text{ }\\text{ }y & x \\\\ -\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}} & \\frac{1}{x}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={\\left(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)}\\right)}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{2y}{x}\\right)}=\\frac{1}{2v}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 5**: Perform the change of variables, and evaluate the integral:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi xy)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{D}{\\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right)}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi xy)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}{v}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi u)|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}{v}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi u)|\\frac{1}{2v}|\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi u)[{\\int }_{1}^{5}v\\,dv]du \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi u){[\\frac{1}{2}\\,{v}^{2}]}_{1}^{5}\\,du \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi u)\\cdot 12\\,du \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi u)\\,du \\\\  & =6{[-\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi u)]}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{\\pi }(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{12}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495170 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a866929-0beb-5a32-8959-34966c6e6ad9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25}\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 12 \\\\ 12 & 16\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494370} {:answer/id #uuid "28cc6daa-99e2-5439-a52d-8c74f6f8d55b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 12 \\\\ 12 & 16\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494393} {:answer/id #uuid "7d73673d-5635-5b93-8b05-960db3e3f68f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}16 & -12 \\\\ -12 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494590} {:answer/id #uuid "891a910a-dee7-5f7a-b066-db75538859fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -12 \\\\ -12 & 16\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494623} {:answer/id #uuid "fec25ec0-ae75-52d4-992b-cbf821a92df5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25}\\begin{bmatrix}16 & -12 \\\\ -12 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494915}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fec25ec0-ae75-52d4-992b-cbf821a92df5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25}\\begin{bmatrix}16 & -12 \\\\ -12 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494915} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f1f6569-2671-58ca-aa36-0fefdf95c894" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494975}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f8b0f486-8442-538c-933a-d85ad556ff51" :question/math-academy-id "q-95716" :question/problem "Find the orthogonal projection matrix that maps $x\\in {R}^{2}$ onto the subspace spanned by an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =1$ of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 12 \\\\ 12 & 17\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "The spectral decomposition of a $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\lambda }_{1}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1}^{T}+{\\lambda }_{2}{u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere ${u}_{1}$ and ${u}_{2}$ are orthonormal eigenvectors of $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2},$ respectively.\n\nMoreover, ${u}_{i}\\cdot {u}_{i}^{T}$ is the projection matrix corresponding to ${u}_{i}.$\n\nFirst, we need to find an eigenvector that corresponds to $\\lambda =1.$ Computing $A-1I,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-I & =\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 12 \\\\ 12 & 17\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 12 \\\\ 12 & 16\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 12 & 0 \\\\ 12 & 16 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\left(-\\frac{4}{3}\\right){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 12 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{4}{3}{x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{4}{3}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting ${x}_{2}=3,$ we get the eigenvector \n\n$$\nv=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwhere $‖v‖=5.$ Dividing $v$ by its norm, we obtain the normalized eigenvector: \n\n$$\nu=\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFinally, the required orthogonal projection matrix is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {u}^{T} & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}\\begin{bmatrix}16 & -12 \\\\ -12 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496226 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51c5dada-d996-51cf-94d1-ca897ceda4c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495696}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51c5dada-d996-51cf-94d1-ca897ceda4c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495696} :answer-field/id #uuid "da300820-d65a-54b5-a122-648e1be4ca42" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496194} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0db68d80-560b-5294-a3e9-812966c11801" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495542}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0db68d80-560b-5294-a3e9-812966c11801" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495542} :answer-field/id #uuid "e16e42d5-5e57-5702-bb36-98fb0bad0dd6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496198}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "07b5302b-d797-5328-827e-aa28a460f929" :question/math-academy-id "q-181149" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4u-6v &=-3 \\\\ u &=-v-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(u,v)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$(u,v)=($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. It so happens that the second equation is already solved for $u:$\n\n$$\nu=-v-2\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $u$ with $-v-2$ in the first equation and solve for $v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4u-6v & =-3 \\\\ 4(-v-2)-6v & =-3 \\\\ -4v-8-6v & =-3 \\\\ -10v & =5 \\\\ v & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $v=-\\frac{1}{2}$ into $u=-v-2,$ then we can find the value of $u:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =-v-2 \\\\ u & =-\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)-2 \\\\ u & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $u=-\\frac{3}{2},\\,v=-\\frac{1}{2},$ which can be expressed as $(-\\frac{3}{2},-\\frac{1}{2}).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496243 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "562298c6-72ee-5938-8d58-eb91a47a9605" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0,3\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495706} {:answer/id #uuid "6caa4140-d1ac-55c9-a193-10e41b581be0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{5\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495750} {:answer/id #uuid "8af47cc7-2ec7-566f-b27b-062280eae539" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0,\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{3\\pi }{2},\\frac{5\\pi }{2},3\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495816} {:answer/id #uuid "dcbb8c12-c911-598d-ab85-055bef131cb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{3\\pi }{2},\\frac{5\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495996} {:answer/id #uuid "f65de3f9-aea8-580f-b207-a07101ca1006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0,\\frac{3\\pi }{2},3\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6caa4140-d1ac-55c9-a193-10e41b581be0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{5\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495750} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b20b945-8756-5419-8b95-3531f4fb01ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496143}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3a2c219c-ccba-5ebb-bb19-2884f7df2aa0" :question/math-academy-id "q-95376" :question/problem "Let $X$ be a random variable with the probability density function shown below. What are the modes of $X?$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+1}{3\\pi +2}, & 0\\le x\\le 3\\pi  \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The modes of a random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ are the values of $x$ at the global maxima of $f(x).$\n\nTo find the global maxima of $f(x),$ we find the critical points of $f(x)$ and then apply the candidates test.\n\nFirst, we find the critical points.\n\n- The piece of $f(x)$ defined on $0\\le x\\le 3\\pi $ is $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+1}{3\\pi +2}.$ Taking the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{3\\pi +2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{3\\pi +2}=0\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+k\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is any integer.\nAmong these critical points, only three lie within the interval $[0,3\\pi ].$ These are $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{3\\pi }{2},\\frac{5\\pi }{2},$ so we keep them all.\n\n- The derivative doesn't exist at the endpoints $x=0,3\\pi .$ So, these are critical points as well.\n\nNow, we evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points $x=0,\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{3\\pi }{2},\\frac{5\\pi }{2},3\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡0+1}{3\\pi +2}=\\frac{1}{3\\pi +2} \\\\ f\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)+1}{3\\pi +2}=\\frac{2}{3\\pi +2} \\\\ f\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\right) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\right)+1}{3\\pi +2}=0 \\\\ f\\left(\\frac{5\\pi }{2}\\right) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{5\\pi }{2}\\right)+1}{3\\pi +2}=\\frac{2}{3\\pi +2} \\\\ f(3\\pi ) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )+1}{3\\pi +2}=\\frac{1}{3\\pi +2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compare all of the values above. The largest values are\n\n$$\nf\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)=f\\left(\\frac{5\\pi }{2}\\right)=\\frac{2}{3\\pi +2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the modes of $X$ are $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $\\frac{5\\pi }{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496249 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2188e8eb-24f6-567f-b4a0-82bd8c14ebf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495582}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2188e8eb-24f6-567f-b4a0-82bd8c14ebf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495582} :answer-field/id #uuid "28157b7f-c2b1-5be6-a604-5bd03e2ba7ef" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496092}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "470fa283-2b00-51e0-9a35-7c42b40fff42" :question/math-academy-id "q-171600" :question/problem "If $\\frac{3k-2}{6}=-(k+2),$ then $k=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying the equation through by $6$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3k-2}{6} & =-(k+2) \\\\ 6\\cdot \\left(\\frac{3k-2}{6}\\right) & =6\\cdot (-(k+2)) \\\\ \\cancel{6}\\cdot \\left(\\frac{3k-2}{\\cancel{6}}\\right) & =-6(k+2) \\\\ 3k-2 & =-6k-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the remaining equation using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3k-2 & =-6k-12 \\\\ 3k-2+6k & =-6k-12+6k \\\\ 9k-2 & =-12 \\\\ 9k-2+2 & =-12+2 \\\\ 9k & =-10 \\\\ \\frac{9k}{9} & =\\frac{-10}{9} \\\\ k & =-\\frac{10}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496261 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d762ea4-afec-5d24-987b-1629fe8078d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{kg}\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}\\,{\\text{s}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495571} {:answer/id #uuid "4cfc7a0e-24fa-511e-8e2a-c033f6a57641" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{kg}\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}}{\\text{s}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495686} {:answer/id #uuid "4ed65f3f-f541-5dbc-b19e-e2762e996517" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{kg}\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495691} {:answer/id #uuid "daaa803f-6528-5c7c-ab17-6235345378e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{kg}\\,\\text{m}\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495993} {:answer/id #uuid "defedfc3-6a0c-570a-8e21-65d713653ddd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{kg}\\,\\text{m}}{\\text{s}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496004}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ed65f3f-f541-5dbc-b19e-e2762e996517" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{kg}\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495691} :answer-field/id #uuid "50db8c22-bd5b-5673-ad8f-e5d45d8e0739" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496112}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5e4a27b0-0664-5456-aded-ea139acd3d27" :question/math-academy-id "q-46155" :question/problem "The work applied to an object is the result of multiplying the force by the distance. Given that the force is measured in Newtons $\\left(\\frac{\\text{kg}\\,\\text{m}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}\\right),$ determine the unit of work in terms of kilograms, meters and seconds." :question/worked-solution "The force is measured in Newtons $\\left(\\frac{\\text{kg}\\,\\text{m}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}\\right)$ and distance is measured in meters ($\\text{m}$). Since the work is the multiplication of force by distance, we must multiply force units by distance units. Thus, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{kg}\\,\\text{m}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}\\cdot \\text{m}=\\frac{\\text{kg}\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nThus, the unit of work is $\\frac{\\text{kg}\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496264 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80350002-a1a3-5d74-bd16-1ec73fee04f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3})$ and $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3})$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495786} {:answer/id #uuid "8f8e83f7-8310-58f5-9c73-52c7cc216ae6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(\\frac{-\\sqrt{2}}{3},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3})$ and $(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3})$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495826} {:answer/id #uuid "9823e226-22f2-5864-b4b5-cc7c8eaef60c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3})$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495852} {:answer/id #uuid "9d651deb-dd53-5f49-8875-9a85b310492f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3})$ and $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3})$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495860} {:answer/id #uuid "ce78662c-56d5-5bd3-8e1e-31dfb2b4b788" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3})$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495958}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d651deb-dd53-5f49-8875-9a85b310492f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3})$ and $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3})$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495860} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1dd5380-2900-5587-97bf-5ddd6b25c63f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496200}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6022ca77-a6e7-5c06-a55c-446e2e02d3c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-71123" :question/problem "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the ellipsoid $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}+3{z}^{2}=1$ and the line \n$\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-t \\\\ y &=t, \\\\ z &=t\\end{aligned}\\right.$ where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting the expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ from the parametric equation of the line into the equation of the ellipsoid, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}+3{z}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+6{z}^{2} & =2 \\\\ (-t)^{2}+2(t)^{2}+6(t)^{2} & =2 \\\\ {t}^{2}+2{t}^{2}+6{t}^{2} & =2 \\\\ 9{t}^{2} & =2 \\\\ {t}^{2} & =\\frac{2}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $t=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}$ and $t=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}.$ \n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ y &=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ z &=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nso the first point is $(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}).$\n\n- For $t=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ y &=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ z &=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nso the second point is $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3})$ and $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496271 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86a95d46-89a3-5b06-8221-b59e68bab013" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "h=\\frac{8}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495801} {:answer/id #uuid "bfd1647f-a339-5240-b787-f6c0d05abdbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "h=-\\frac{7}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495931} {:answer/id #uuid "e273f529-d3a2-5eba-a46e-b61afe82fb5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "h=\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496011} {:answer/id #uuid "f9adebf3-6330-575d-845f-896e038bb897" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "h=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496054} {:answer/id #uuid "f9eecf5b-4431-5988-ac24-8ec51e2c687c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "h=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496057}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86a95d46-89a3-5b06-8221-b59e68bab013" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "h=\\frac{8}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495801} :answer-field/id #uuid "14966880-3ea7-59e7-a17e-fec0ac900176" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496083}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6bdf897b-5216-5fe0-b918-3faeb980f813" :question/math-academy-id "q-104472" :question/problem "Solve for $h$ where $\\frac{3h-4}{2}=2-h.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying both sides by $2.$ We must make sure that all of the terms on the right-hand side are multiplied by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3h-4}{2} & =2-h \\\\ 2\\cdot \\left(\\frac{3h-4}{2}\\right) & =2\\cdot (2-h) \\\\ \\cancel{2}\\cdot \\left(\\frac{3h-4}{\\cancel{2}}\\right) & =2\\cdot 2-2\\cdot h \\\\ 3h-4 & =4-2h\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the remaining equation using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3h-4 & =4-2h \\\\ 3h-4+2h & =4-2h+2h \\\\ 5h-4 & =4 \\\\ 5h-4+4 & =4+4 \\\\ 5h & =8 \\\\ \\frac{5h}{5} & =\\frac{8}{5} \\\\ h & =\\frac{8}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496277 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "290bfc84-e444-5079-8d18-8f0f58f4d969" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{11}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495600} {:answer/id #uuid "37c0081c-72ea-53b5-830f-01d721471189" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{22}{45}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495642} {:answer/id #uuid "95839550-f140-5f9e-a1e5-8aa2c82702bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{45}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495842} {:answer/id #uuid "aaf85b04-9f5b-52ba-8d31-f3f78566da82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{25}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495892} {:answer/id #uuid "b62f4a13-9b15-5386-ab05-2a22a1b14183" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{45}{22}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aaf85b04-9f5b-52ba-8d31-f3f78566da82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{25}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495892} :answer-field/id #uuid "e82146a9-b8b1-5e83-aeec-05796f3d090e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496203}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7e49ab95-b651-5531-ac5c-90e4392b7705" :question/math-academy-id "q-31686" :question/problem "Solve for $x$ where $\\frac{5-x}{3}=7x-15.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying the equation through by $7$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5-x}{3} & =7x-15 \\\\ 3\\left(\\frac{5-x}{3}\\right) & =3(7x-15) \\\\ \\cancel{3}\\left(\\frac{5-x}{\\cancel{3}}\\right) & =21x-45 \\\\ 5-x & =21x-45\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the remaining equation using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5-x & =21x-45 \\\\ 5-x+x & =21x-45+x \\\\ 5 & =22x-45 \\\\ 5+45 & =22x-45+45 \\\\ 50 & =22x \\\\ \\frac{50}{22} & =\\frac{22x}{22} \\\\ \\frac{25}{11} & =\\frac{\\cancel{22}x}{\\cancel{22}} \\\\ x & =\\frac{25}{11}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496280 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a31c016-7581-51c5-822b-4a571829ce10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{in}}{\\text{s}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495535} {:answer/id #uuid "70cfc503-22ee-55c2-836b-3453b0c8c7f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{m}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495757} {:answer/id #uuid "92f01d15-91dc-5198-9880-f2fea86ce575" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\text{m}}^{2}}{\\text{s}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495834} {:answer/id #uuid "a785465d-4be2-52e9-bd6a-046a7ecc4c55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{s}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495886} {:answer/id #uuid "f747453d-9a93-50ac-912e-3072a4460dcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{in}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496050}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70cfc503-22ee-55c2-836b-3453b0c8c7f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{m}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495757} :answer-field/id #uuid "5165db33-f994-5bf2-a4e5-e80f00f1780e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496113}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "84dd0eb1-204d-5088-96b6-0cbdfd5aaddf" :question/math-academy-id "q-103391" :question/problem "John is traveling in the subway and wants to determine how the subway speed changes as time goes on. What are appropriate units for the rate of change of the speed, in terms of base units?" :question/worked-solution "We *measure the change* in the speed, as *we change* the time. Consequently, any appropriate unit must take the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{unit of speed}}{\\text{unit of time}}.\n$$\n\nIn terms of meters and seconds, the unit for speed is $\\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{s}},$ and the unit for time is $\\text{s}.$ Therefore, the appropriate unit for the rate of change of speed is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\left(\\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{s}}\\right)}{\\text{s}}=\\frac{\\text{m}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nor, meters per square second."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496282 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2903bd31-59f2-5edf-ba78-0b700636216f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495599} {:answer/id #uuid "72fcd5f6-74c1-548c-b798-b9f86c8b5a52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495763} {:answer/id #uuid "d9e331d6-2b84-5961-a705-7c0440233497" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495990} {:answer/id #uuid "e4145407-31af-5f0e-be8b-a08fc7a69e9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496016} {:answer/id #uuid "e87b73a0-162f-5a86-8eb0-04ffa6648475" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{8}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9e331d6-2b84-5961-a705-7c0440233497" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495990} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac07d115-2c5e-5c77-b205-49ff29ccdb65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496158}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c16a549-c615-5f5a-9201-b01b9bbc4908" :question/math-academy-id "q-36325" :question/problem "Find the projection of the intersection between the hyperboloid of one sheet \n$(x+3)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-2{z}^{2}=1$\n and the plane   $x+2z=-3$ onto the\n$xy$-plane." :question/worked-solution "Since we want to find the projection onto the $xy$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $z.$ First, we solve the equation of the plane for $z$, as follows:\n\n$$\nx+2z=-3\\,⟹\\,z=-\\frac{x+3}{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $z$ into the equation of the hyperboloid, we obtain: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-2{\\left(-\\frac{x+3}{2}\\right)}^{2} & =1 \\\\ (x+3)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{2} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the projection of the intersection is the ellipse $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{2}=1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496290 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fce19de-60b6-585b-a388-1fa1eeb5a3ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{kg}\\,\\text{m}}{\\text{s}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495694} {:answer/id #uuid "79a01367-cc89-5f4a-869f-97de82fd3129" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\text{m}\\,{\\text{s}}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495771} {:answer/id #uuid "7f0d7771-34e6-5d10-a9a3-70e0207f524d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{kg}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495782} {:answer/id #uuid "894020f7-35dc-5ea3-907a-86bdf3be687c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{kg}\\,\\text{s}}{\\text{m}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495809} {:answer/id #uuid "ac5ce8dc-668f-526f-89a8-3f0762530def" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{kg}\\,\\text{m}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495895}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac5ce8dc-668f-526f-89a8-3f0762530def" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{kg}\\,\\text{m}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495895} :answer-field/id #uuid "f644e2e4-a4d8-546c-9e9b-b5558284b434" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496213}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9d7c30aa-a3e9-5b45-be5b-cfccc139072e" :question/math-academy-id "q-105397" :question/problem "The magnitude of a force $F$ applied to an object is related to the work $W$ and the distance $d$ by the formula $F=\\frac{W}{d}.$  Given that $W$ is measured in $\\frac{\\text{kg}\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}$ and the distance is measured in meters, determine an appropriate measurement unit for the force." :question/worked-solution "To find the unit of the force, we substitute the given units of work and distance into the formula and simplify.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =\\frac{W}{d} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\left(\\frac{\\text{kg}\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}\\right)}{\\text{m}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{m}}\\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\text{kg}\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}}{\\text{m}\\cdot {\\text{s}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{kg}\\cdot \\cancel{\\text{m}}\\cdot \\text{m}}{\\cancel{\\text{m}}\\cdot {\\text{s}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{kg}\\,\\text{m}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the unit of the force is $\\frac{\\text{kg}\\,\\text{m}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496331 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14976fe2-9b52-5ebe-8c73-8ff28cb9c14c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{s}\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}}{{\\text{kg}}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495554} {:answer/id #uuid "7c54496e-2150-55be-ad11-f0813a6820d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{kg}\\,\\text{m}\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495776} {:answer/id #uuid "b6d75902-8118-5803-a45a-9a41127624e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{kg}\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495920} {:answer/id #uuid "c72b361b-647a-5fbe-98d9-e79fe7657b16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{kg}\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}\\,{\\text{s}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495945} {:answer/id #uuid "fb4b5f65-0be1-558d-93d2-208a32c43b71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{kg}\\,\\text{m}}{\\text{s}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6d75902-8118-5803-a45a-9a41127624e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{kg}\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495920} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c9253cc-52ac-5d1c-b3ee-ba5595fbaccc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496132}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f927f6ff-ccc6-56f9-848c-de38a72fd309" :question/math-academy-id "q-46081" :question/problem "The work $W$ applied to a body is related to force $F$ and distance $d$ by the equation $W=F\\cdot d.$ If $F$ is measured in Newtons $\\left(\\frac{\\text{kg}\\,\\text{m}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}\\right)$ and $d$ is measured in meters, what is an appropriate measurement unit for work?" :question/worked-solution "To find the unit of work, we substitute the given units of force and distance into the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W & =F\\cdot d \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{kg}\\,\\text{m}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}\\cdot \\text{m} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{kg}\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the unit of work is $\\frac{\\text{kg}\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496333 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fb757b8-2149-526a-af68-c96954680eb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495548} {:answer/id #uuid "7d66aa7f-6693-5615-970b-c7da91b05cd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495778} {:answer/id #uuid "9c952b49-23cd-5299-ab3b-0fd0ba05087c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495857} {:answer/id #uuid "9ee350b8-cb7d-5d53-877e-b380e44154a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495865} {:answer/id #uuid "a4d94021-52b3-52e5-909c-4f0d63cad22c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495880}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ee350b8-cb7d-5d53-877e-b380e44154a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495865} :answer-field/id #uuid "3de57bae-a1f3-5ae4-b2cb-ef29b2469101" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496099}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fcf291ca-08c9-536b-b233-ba6182878dc7" :question/math-academy-id "q-44329" :question/problem "Solve for $t$ where $-2t=\\frac{4-6t}{9}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying the equation through by $9$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2t & =\\frac{4-6t}{9} \\\\ \\frac{4-6t}{9} & =-2t \\\\ 9\\left(\\frac{4-6t}{9}\\right) & =9(-2t) \\\\ \\cancel{9}\\left(\\frac{4-6t}{\\cancel{9}}\\right) & =-18t \\\\ 4-6t & =-18t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the remaining equation using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4-6t & =-18t \\\\ 4-6t+6t & =-18t+6t \\\\ 4 & =-12t \\\\ -12t & =4 \\\\ \\frac{-12t}{-12} & =\\frac{4}{-12} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-12}t}{\\cancel{-12}} & =-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ t & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496407 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19a3ecd7-a741-5deb-abdc-1ecdb08d7f86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a1/a1436e6273de88dd0f122f0142dd3157db2ec007fb7670aaa555969bbb7adeed.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496396} {:answer/id #uuid "8e2c04fb-8750-5cb5-b025-5eb00c605645" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e7/e76046e12180d9892dacb64c0c2669ced875271819e756f822550f10fb77fb45.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496413} {:answer/id #uuid "9ecdde9b-858a-5b1b-8851-f76f0b3930d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/84/84bf7d020c65bebbe23fb8d2dd7e919a3a1ac2ab27978c91cbe89973085aeb43.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496415} {:answer/id #uuid "ce3bfefe-920a-5618-a806-1b47b244864b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fe/fee181bd159fe9d1fbe615bed1ef9b7eddc424342d473432725d468ac9df6d5f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496426} {:answer/id #uuid "f747cbad-15f5-5530-ade3-1e452e56a875" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bb/bb8a9db0e8d8c91c6f4296b21aef84a242b989b4257e3cef3282adf5174ed079.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19a3ecd7-a741-5deb-abdc-1ecdb08d7f86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a1/a1436e6273de88dd0f122f0142dd3157db2ec007fb7670aaa555969bbb7adeed.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496396} :answer-field/id #uuid "59fa873c-1ad6-5952-be17-ba65dbd1e41d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496411}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "408bf66a-2a8e-5c7e-aa05-3b6725a15b53" :question/problem "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- \\frac{9 \\left(x + 2\\right)^{2}}{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\left(- \\frac{9 \\left(x + 2\\right)^{2}}{2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =- \\frac{9}{2}\\int \\left(x + 2\\right)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =- \\frac{9}{2}\\left(\\frac{\\left(x + 2\\right)^{3}}{3}\\right)+C \\\\ y & =- \\frac{3 \\left(x + 2\\right)^{3}}{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-2,0,2.$\n\n![](images/f0/f0abc54ee55826263306f014480e9a4d36c4d0d3fd10b4c51757d03f38d00ae6.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496418 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4969ec6c-e9f4-588d-8add-22b688d7f5e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/df/dfde7e57d4f1ccff20d93f1d8144e0b3df5831d7be121bce5911582cdc360c79.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496408} {:answer/id #uuid "4fb5e34e-5cad-5d3e-bffd-d4db835005ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a0/a083eb2f43215be1f455bdafa6cd9aacb41398f1053dd0cd6f364ba3fa3be81b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496409} {:answer/id #uuid "b26f3d57-e630-51f3-9bc9-154b97e12f9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/07/07ae2a857f849aefebc75fc578c868758000d692846a52d0cd190f201c9f57d5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496419} {:answer/id #uuid "b9a2998e-5a7f-57ba-842a-0b21ee853acb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/24/243a57e77d376e6c285707e9beaac8d3f3573f61b9dbde964e5af31444999cd3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496423} {:answer/id #uuid "d08e1882-463f-5601-9691-95d1fcf45eee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5f/5fa542eb74b8d4b04e199ccfa0598304af38aa69ab59bb84a5873736aeb53842.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496427}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d08e1882-463f-5601-9691-95d1fcf45eee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5f/5fa542eb74b8d4b04e199ccfa0598304af38aa69ab59bb84a5873736aeb53842.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496427} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc165c51-9611-50a2-b0e8-171538697c81" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496438}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "aef084ac-c810-558a-a0b5-af2b0b066444" :question/problem "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{9 \\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\left(\\frac{9 \\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}}{2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{9}{2}\\int \\left(x - 2\\right)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}\\left(\\frac{\\left(x - 2\\right)^{3}}{3}\\right)+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{3 \\left(x - 2\\right)^{3}}{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-2,0,2.$\n\n![](images/12/1235c9c0d6913436949a82342c89149bcd494498e6bbfd10c69aecb6b471c5c6.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496429 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d6a1146-7f52-5c21-8481-707664564a73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/42/423249f8b6972f7f9c7482f5ccd8c1fa6f786ee7f4b7e8381fb9d552e65fb5fe.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496397} {:answer/id #uuid "2e1e8205-a3a1-54f9-be35-36c48fa91e07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d7/d79f542f2d7066f0d08c935ee07eb17f12bdb4bc03b0d50a9b3b55f493ef3fbd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496402} {:answer/id #uuid "a81f77a2-6dd5-5d7a-88bf-ba50595b238d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e9/e9bf393362331bba0ce4cd1ad2f85bc300c340eac451b3e44cf9a7d82c1a519d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496417} {:answer/id #uuid "cbb2d373-4142-52a2-8286-325b9784e2e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/92/9239d5fa24b4470527313e87be01cdfa12511a0bb5008bc8a1584b018b9faf66.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496425} {:answer/id #uuid "f4bfb58f-2a48-58c7-8f84-d943df4fff49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e6/e6497eec57bbd7a05803dc6218a2cb0363becc62b41c19cb3d90d701ebacc801.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496435}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d6a1146-7f52-5c21-8481-707664564a73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/42/423249f8b6972f7f9c7482f5ccd8c1fa6f786ee7f4b7e8381fb9d552e65fb5fe.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496397} :answer-field/id #uuid "18683a5e-c88e-55e8-bf18-3022667e5c68" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496395}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d592e808-7510-5a65-9880-a1f40ab32589" :question/problem "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{e^{- \\frac{x}{4}}}{8}?$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\left(\\frac{e^{- \\frac{x}{4}}}{8}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{8}\\int e^{- \\frac{x}{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\left(- 4 e^{- \\frac{x}{4}}\\right)+C \\\\ y & =- \\frac{e^{- \\frac{x}{4}}}{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-2,0,2.$\n\n![](images/25/258e0e2dea305737216c1a4cbc8f448d93055b1c97eb8b8e73805b7fb8425c73.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496432 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0229aff1-dd15-5dc0-8c29-4fe7230b6c3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/66/66c0cf6892e6d86094f6ce2cbebb03fde5b72b62142502eb7df37b189fe1e090.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496391} {:answer/id #uuid "25995fff-b334-5513-a18b-186af48cae46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e7/e713f3dec38a143e0262ba7ebac0e654abf2bda07e5c9f05fdd0f98159a3af3d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496398} {:answer/id #uuid "2d1495df-de65-5c2a-808e-c395b77f25c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3e/3e72325c08bf00f7ba5c76370b4be967249bb359cb4c8f106a5341192ec65be4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496401} {:answer/id #uuid "51af2964-ab37-58f8-bfb2-3440d159b7cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8f/8f7920be5fb2d5b085400b14ecaeaa9f48a1bfcd5574b26846d67d2d24998bac.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496410} {:answer/id #uuid "e47a143e-9a2a-504a-abb4-4687e24cbda0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d6/d6b9688cbe10695bcce92a75e8cb732370ff826697e340648e6b1e62114c61ca.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496431}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25995fff-b334-5513-a18b-186af48cae46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e7/e713f3dec38a143e0262ba7ebac0e654abf2bda07e5c9f05fdd0f98159a3af3d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496398} :answer-field/id #uuid "db6badbb-63b1-5ae0-86a4-973b3f656302" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496430}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ebcdfba8-83b2-550e-83cd-6936094d4ac7" :question/problem "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{4 e^{- \\frac{2 x}{3}}}{9}?$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\left(\\frac{4 e^{- \\frac{2 x}{3}}}{9}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{4}{9}\\int e^{- \\frac{2 x}{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}\\left(- \\frac{3 e^{- \\frac{2 x}{3}}}{2}\\right)+C \\\\ y & =- \\frac{2 e^{- \\frac{2 x}{3}}}{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-2,0,2.$\n\n![](images/ae/ae0e43d8605937216fd9b02d433085e87cf87e6f3bc66f3b8d0d20a86aada3d2.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496445 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17b7a9ee-05d2-5e22-9972-601b4fb37512" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=- \\frac{3 \\cdot 2^{x}}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}^{2}} + C x + D + \\frac{5 x^{3}}{6} - 8 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496443} {:answer/id #uuid "98586e82-d740-5cdf-8e68-aec82060ba46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=- \\frac{3 \\cdot 2^{x}}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}^{2}} + D + \\frac{5 x^{3}}{6} - 8 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496467} {:answer/id #uuid "a45dd023-ac47-5719-bfa2-a56d75067b69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=- \\frac{3 \\cdot 2^{x}}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}^{2}} + C x + \\frac{5 x^{3}}{6} - 8 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496471} {:answer/id #uuid "e06fa046-2cc1-520d-ad5d-71c843cfdecd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=- \\frac{3 \\cdot 2^{x}}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}} + C x + D + \\frac{5 x^{2}}{2} - 4 \\cos{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496480} {:answer/id #uuid "ef279cf5-32e4-53ca-b8a9-ca1692cb44ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{3 \\cdot 2^{x}}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}^{2}} + C x + D - \\frac{5 x^{3}}{6} + 8 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17b7a9ee-05d2-5e22-9972-601b4fb37512" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=- \\frac{3 \\cdot 2^{x}}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}^{2}} + C x + D + \\frac{5 x^{3}}{6} - 8 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496443} :answer-field/id #uuid "f54355e5-1536-513f-be27-f9963dda5050" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496487}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2a8c21f0-1469-51c6-8b1e-9df019a179b7" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n4\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=- 12 \\cdot 2^{x} + 20 x + 8 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=- 3 \\cdot 2^{x} + 5 x + 2 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\left(- 3 \\cdot 2^{x} + 5 x + 2 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =((5)\\int \\left(x\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) + ((-3)\\int \\left(2^{x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) + ((2)\\int \\left(\\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =((5)\\left(\\frac{x^{2}}{2}\\right)) + ((-3)\\left(\\frac{2^{x}}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}\\right)) + ((2)\\left(- 2 \\cos{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}\\right))+C \\\\  & =- \\frac{3 \\cdot 2^{x}}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}} + C + \\frac{5 x^{2}}{2} - 4 \\cos{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\left(- \\frac{3 \\cdot 2^{x}}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}} + C + \\frac{5 x^{2}}{2} - 4 \\cos{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =(\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)\\int \\left(x^{2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) + (\\left(- \\frac{3}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}\\right)\\int \\left(2^{x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) + ((-4)\\int \\left(\\cos{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x)+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{x^{3}}{3}\\right)) + (\\left(- \\frac{3}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}\\right)\\left(\\frac{2^{x}}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}\\right)) + ((-4)\\left(2 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}\\right))+Cx+D \\\\  & =- \\frac{3 \\cdot 2^{x}}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}^{2}} + C x + D + \\frac{5 x^{3}}{6} - 8 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496457 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a018671-33dd-5e1e-a486-47ea10f91d83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=D - \\frac{x^{3}}{6} - \\frac{7 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4} - 2 e^{- 2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496446} {:answer/id #uuid "96e035ed-98be-559e-afe9-4fdf3c466757" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + D - \\frac{x^{2}}{2} + \\frac{7 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2} + 4 e^{- 2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496465} {:answer/id #uuid "98d9400f-9d5a-5d32-9ef8-18683c25276d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x - \\frac{x^{3}}{6} - \\frac{7 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4} - 2 e^{- 2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496468} {:answer/id #uuid "9d88d181-065b-5b99-9c3d-def935f9acf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + D - \\frac{x^{3}}{6} - \\frac{7 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4} - 2 e^{- 2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496470} {:answer/id #uuid "ab12cfcf-d837-5893-98cc-7bf52f85922b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + D + \\frac{x^{3}}{6} + \\frac{7 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4} + 2 e^{- 2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d88d181-065b-5b99-9c3d-def935f9acf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + D - \\frac{x^{3}}{6} - \\frac{7 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4} - 2 e^{- 2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496470} :answer-field/id #uuid "c862d365-4036-51de-9a7d-af7d82638b2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496476}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "64d2112b-6455-564b-a00e-e1e0242afaf1" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=- 2 x + 14 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} - 16 e^{- 2 x}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=- x + 7 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} - 8 e^{- 2 x}.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\left(- x + 7 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} - 8 e^{- 2 x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =((-1)\\int \\left(x\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) + ((-8)\\int \\left(e^{- 2 x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) + ((7)\\int \\left(\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =((-1)\\left(\\frac{x^{2}}{2}\\right)) + ((-8)\\left(- \\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{2}\\right)) + ((7)\\left(\\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}\\right))+C \\\\  & =C - \\frac{x^{2}}{2} + \\frac{7 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2} + 4 e^{- 2 x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\left(C - \\frac{x^{2}}{2} + \\frac{7 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2} + 4 e^{- 2 x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =(\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\int \\left(x^{2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) + ((4)\\int \\left(e^{- 2 x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) + (\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right)\\int \\left(\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x)+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{x^{3}}{3}\\right)) + ((4)\\left(- \\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{2}\\right)) + (\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right)\\left(- \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}\\right))+Cx+D \\\\  & =C x + D - \\frac{x^{3}}{6} - \\frac{7 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4} - 2 e^{- 2 x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496459 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47d92b48-ec79-52ab-a285-33d507f81dd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + D - \\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496449} {:answer/id #uuid "7b45ba37-d4e1-534a-a901-557a1c17a7d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.typ